  <h2>Not legal advice</h2>
  <p>
    Better Leasehold publishes general guidance about residential leasehold law in England and
    Wales. It is not legal advice and does not create a solicitor-client or adviser relationship.
    Every block and lease is different, and statutory notices can fail on small technical
    defects.
  </p>

  <h2>Accuracy</h2>
  <p>
    We work to keep the guidance accurate and give the date the law was last checked on each
    guide. The law changes, though, and the guides have not yet been reviewed by a solicitor. We
    cannot guarantee the content is complete, correct or up to date, so please check the sources
    linked on each page.
  </p>

  <h2>Our responsibility</h2>
  <p>
    You use the information on this site at your own risk. We are not responsible for any loss
    arising from relying on it. Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited
    by law.
  </p>

